--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GRANT OF LICENSE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement and the valid provisioning
of an offline node-locked cryptographic license token ("license.token"), Licensor
grants to Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to install
and operate the Software solely on authorized kiosk terminal hardware.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. NODE-LOCKED LICENSING & HARDWARE BINDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
a. The Software incorporates an offline cryptographic node-locking mechanism
   that ties execution to specific physical hardware identifiers (HardwareId)
   derived from the host machine's motherboard, processor, and BIOS.
b. Any attempt to tamper with, forge, decrypt, reverse engineer, or bypass the
   cryptographic verification of `license.token` or the underlying ECDSA/RSA
   verification routines is strictly prohibited and constitutes a material breach
   terminating this license immediately.
c. Machine migration or hardware replacement requires generating an updated
   authorized node-locked token for the new hardware signature.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. PERIPHERAL HARDWARE & INTEGRATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software includes Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) drivers and bridges for:
- Thermal Receipt Printers (Epson EU-m30, TM-m30, TM-T88, Standard ESC/POS)
- Optical Barcode & 2D Scanners (Datalogic Gryphon, QuickScan USB/COM)
- Cash Acceptors, Validators & Recyclers (ITL NV200, NV11, Spectral via REST bridge)
- Payment Terminal QR Gateways (Bakong KHQR, Dynamic Payment QR)

Licensee is responsible for ensuring peripheral hardware compatibility, correct
physical cabling, COM port assignment, and power supply standards.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. DUAL-CURRENCY TRANSACTIONS & FINANCIAL RECORDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software includes dual-currency (USD / KHR) calculation and ledger recording
features. Licensee is responsible for configuring accurate exchange rates and
verifying local legal and fiscal tax compliance for receipts generated by the
Software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Licensee shall NOT:
a. Decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer any compiled binaries of the Software.
b. Rent, lease, lend, sub-license, or redistribute the Software to any third party
   without prior written authorization from Licensor.
c. Remove or alter any copyright, trademark, or proprietary notices from any part
   of the Software, its branding assets, or documentation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. DATA PRIVACY AND SECURITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software is designed with offline-first local SQLCipher database encryption.
Licensee is solely responsible for maintaining physical security of the kiosk
terminal, administrative PIN credentials, and offline database backups.

